Q: How to check if today is between end and start date? A: <p>That didn't work for me either, but this did.</p>
<pre><code>if DateTime.Date( DateTime.LocalNow() ) &gt;= [DeliveryDate] and DateTime.Date( DateTime.LocalNow() ) &lt;= [Finish] then &quot;True&quot; else &quot;False&quot;
</code></pre>

Q: SCSS Dynamically assign margin based on another element A: <p>I had a same query, where I needed to make sure margin-left of sibling element is equal to the width of sibling1. In SCSS, there is no mechanism as such.</p>
<p>So, using JavaScript I did it.</p>
<pre><code> /** 4.--- JS Code to give width --- */
  const authorFirstName = document.querySelector(
    '.author-details-global .field--name-field-user-first-name',
  );
  const authorLastName = document.querySelector(
    '.author-details-global .field--name-field-user-last-name',
  );

  const authorFirstWidth = authorFirstName.getBoundingClientRect().width;
  console.log('**************');
  console.log(`${authorFirstWidth + 3}px`);
  authorLastName.style.marginLeft = `${authorFirstWidth + 3}px`;
</code></pre>
<p>You may use your selectors and use the same method to get the desired results</p>
